Bth_St8~BQNN01000001.1	NCBI/DDBJ	transcript	1710149	1712497	.	-	0	gene_id "CE91St8_12060"; transcript_id "CE91St8_12060"; gene_name "topA"; product "DNA topoisomerase 1"; strain "Bth_St8"; biotype "CDS"; annot_source "NCBI/DDBJ"; protein_id "GKH19471.1"; parent_gene_id ""; mappability "0.6273"; top_confused_with "Bth_VPI"; KEGG_ko "ko:K03168"; KEGG_Pathway "NA"; KEGG_Module "NA"; COG_category "L"; CAZy "NA"; PFAMs "Topoisom_bac,Toprim,Toprim_C_rpt"; EC "5.99.1.2"; Preferred_name "topA"; Description "Releases the supercoiling and torsional tension of DNA, which is introduced during the DNA replication and transcription, by transiently cleaving and rejoining one strand of the DNA duplex. Introduces a single-strand break via transesterification at a target site in duplex DNA. The scissile phosphodiester is attacked by the catalytic tyrosine of the enzyme, resulting in the formation of a DNA-(5'-phosphotyrosyl)-enzyme intermediate and the expulsion of a 3'-OH DNA strand. The free DNA strand then undergoes passage around the unbroken strand, thus removing DNA supercoils. Finally, in the religation step, the DNA 3'-OH attacks the covalent intermediate to expel the active-site tyrosine and restore the DNA phosphodiester backbone"; exclude_from_DE "False";
