Bth_St8~BQNN01000001.1	NCBI/DDBJ	transcript	1873722	1875065	.	+	0	gene_id "CE91St8_13370"; transcript_id "CE91St8_13370"; gene_name "secY"; product "protein translocase subunit SecY"; strain "Bth_St8"; biotype "CDS"; annot_source "NCBI/DDBJ"; protein_id "GKH19602.1"; parent_gene_id ""; mappability "0.1167"; top_confused_with "Bth_VPI"; KEGG_ko "ko:K03076"; KEGG_Pathway "ko02024,ko03060,ko03070,map02024,map03060,map03070"; KEGG_Module "M00335"; COG_category "U"; CAZy "NA"; PFAMs "SecY"; EC "NA"; Preferred_name "secY"; Description "The central subunit of the protein translocation channel SecYEG. Consists of two halves formed by TMs 1-5 and 6-10. These two domains form a lateral gate at the front which open onto the bilayer between TMs 2 and 7, and are clamped together by SecE at the back. The channel is closed by both a pore ring composed of hydrophobic SecY resides and a short helix (helix 2A) on the extracellular side of the membrane which forms a plug. The plug probably moves laterally to allow the channel to open. The ring and the pore may move independently"; exclude_from_DE "False";
